SUMMARY:Forsythe (Brigantine) NWR
DESCRIPTION:Forsythe NWR is one of the best all-around birding spots in the state. “Brig’s” combination of habitats\, easy accessibility\, and penchant for attracting rare species make this a perennial favorite. Expect a wide range of species from long-legged wading birds to raptors\, plus shorebirds and passerines.  Restrooms on site. Led by Mike Mandracchia and Hank Burk. \nLocation: 800 Great Creek Road\, Oceanville\, Forsythe NWR at main lot by headquarters. \nPRE-REGISTRATION REQUIRED \nCOST: $25 Members\, $30 Non-members \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://njaudubon.org/event/forsythe-brigantine-nwr-80/
LOCATION:Edwin B Forsythe National Wildlife Refuge Admin Building And Visitor Contact Station\, 800 Great Creek Road\, Galloway\, NJ\, 08205\, United States
CATEGORIES:All Things Birds,Bird Walk,Birding
